# L §6.1: "same also joins two rows or movements inside one model, in a version" (and L §5.3's version item: "two rows
# that state one movement"). Round 14 (L §6.1): "A same in a version that names a kind or a thing is refused
# (LOAD-SAME): only the header joins them, since an identity isn't dated". (Writer 7.)
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source bank_export "wyciąg"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed

version opening_2026
  cite bank_export
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "saldo"

version statement_01
  cite bank_export
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-01
  covers konto
  bank[r31] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 31"
  bank[r32] = (on: 2026-01-12, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 100.00 PLN) "line 32"
  same konto = world

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME same konto = world in a version names a kind or a thing ...
